  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nUpper-level ridging, warm temperatures, clear skies, and calm winds \nwill continue Thursday and Friday. Temperatures 10 to 20 degrees \nabove normal will be seen across the area on these days. A drastic \npattern change is forecast over the weekend, with an upper-level \ntrough moving through the Pacific Northwest. Winds will start to \npick up on Friday across the higher terrain, with gusts 20 to 30 \nmph. The trough will push a cold front through the area on Saturday, \nbringing cooler temperatures and breezy conditions into the lower \nvalleys as well. Highs are forecast to cool by 10 to 15 degrees from \nFriday, but ensemble variability in the timing of the front reduces \nconfidence in the temperature forecast for Saturday. The trough is \nfavored to deepen over the Pacific Northwest and is becoming \nincreasingly likely to move overhead as a closed low into early next \nweek. This will continue the cooling trend on Sunday and Monday. A \nchance of precipitation will develop especially east of the low with \na 20-40% chance of rain and high mountain snow across central/south \ncentral Idaho, and a 10-20% chance further west. Winds will remain \nbreezy under this pattern.",
